%%label III. Scherzo. Allegro molto
%%note A terse scherzo built from the quartet's four-note cell (A, B flat, C sharp, D) thrown between the instruments in two-bar shards, with off-beat accents, hemiolas and bars of silence; the trio in D major turns the cell into a rising rustic tune over an open-string drone.
X:1
T:Beethoven’s Missing Quartet
T:III. Scherzo. Allegro molto
C:Lor, in the manner of Beethoven
M:3/4
L:1/8
Q:"Allegro molto" 3/4=84
%%score [1 | 2 | 3 | 4]
V:1 clef=treble name="Vl. I"
V:2 clef=treble name="Vl. II"
V:3 clef=alto name="Vla."
V:4 clef=bass name="Vc."
K:Dm
V:1
%%MIDI program 40
V:2
%%MIDI program 40
V:3
%%MIDI program 41
V:4
%%MIDI program 42
% ---- SCHERZO a, bars 1-8: the cell as a two-bar motto, low strings; answered on E by the violins; tutti; hemiola to the cadence
